Request Controller action /t/tracker/project Project.view(ctx) /t/tracker/project/edit?id=7 Project.edit(ctx) /t/tracker/project/save Project.save(ctx) /other/t/tracker/project Other configured application's Project.view(ctx) <p>The normal default action is <code>view</code>. The request parameter <code>d_action</code> can select the action too. Give every public action an explicit policy, and prefix internal helpers with <code>_</code> so they cannot be invoked as routes.</p> <pre><code>class Example(object):
    ACCESS_POLICY = {"view": "authenticated", "save": "authenticated"}

    def view(self, ctx):
        ctx.go_to = "/t/web/hello"

    def save(self, ctx):
        """POST"""
        # Validate first, then save and redirect.
        ctx.go_to = ctx.ctxPath + "/t/web/hello"

    def _normalize(self, value):
        return (value or "").strip()
</code></pre> <p>For mutation actions, the docstring must start exactly with <code>POST</code>, <code>PUT</code>, or <code>DELETE</code>. The engine checks these prefixes for explicitly selected actions. A <code>GET</code> docstring is not a general GET-only guard; keep <code>view</code> read-only. Use POST forms for tutorial writes and deletions.</p>
